					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-627637#post-1792638</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-627637/s-c-plastics-hub#post-1792638</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Sun, 09 Jun 2013 04:45:10 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Ihp</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>1267048</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <blockquote> <p>So how did the Foundation find them?</p> </blockquote> <p>If you've read the rest, the Camp Krakkow incident was the thing that established S &amp; C Plastics in the town. After that, they noticed all sorts of other weird shit happening.</p> <blockquote> <p>And why aren't the Foundation researchers located there likewise affected?</p> </blockquote> <p>Note the &quot;unless it's tourist season&quot; caveat. People who are native to Sloth Spit don't notice because they've gotten used to living with weird-ass shit, but people who are from out of town will probably find something odd about Main Street losing gravity for 3 seconds every day at 2:13 P.M.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-627637#post-1792631</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-627637/s-c-plastics-hub#post-1792631</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Sun, 09 Jun 2013 04:35:15 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Khym Chanur</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>163438</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <blockquote> <p>No matter what, a nexus is like Vegas: what happens there stays there. No anomalous event that occur in a nexus zone ever leaves. Likewise, the outside world will be largely ignorant of what happens in the nexus.</p> </blockquote> <p>So how did the Foundation find them?</p> <blockquote> <p>The population never notices, or if it does, it really doesn't give a shit. This is a large boon to the Foundation, as amnestics require no administration, unless it's tourist season.</p> </blockquote> <p>And why aren't the Foundation researchers located there likewise affected?</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
